# Secrets
# .env itself is tracked on purpose — Lovable manages it and it holds only
# publishable values (Supabase URL, project id, anon key), all of which ship
# in the browser bundle anyway.
#
# ANY REAL SECRET GOES IN .env.local, WHICH IS NEVER COMMITTED.
# That means the Unsplash access key, Stripe secret key, service_role key,
# and anything else that must not be public. Vite loads .env.local after .env
# and it takes precedence, so it also works for overriding values locally.
.env.local
.env.*.local
.env.production

# `.env` itself is TRACKED in this repo and must stay that way: Lovable writes
# the Supabase URL and publishable key there, and those are public by design
# (the anon key is shipped to every browser and is protected by RLS).
#
# THE TRAP: because it is tracked, anything you add to that file gets committed
# and pushed to GitHub. Never put a secret in it. Specifically:
#
#   STRIPE_SECRET_KEY        <- goes in Lovable project settings, never a file
#   STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET    <- same
#   SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY <- same, this one bypasses every RLS policy
#
# A leaked Stripe secret key lets anyone charge your customers and read your
# payment history, and it is live from the moment it lands in a public repo.
# If one is ever committed, rotate it in Stripe first and clean the history
# second: the rotation is what actually stops the bleeding.
.env.secret
.env.server

